## Oracle finding

Pinned Java `ProcessQueue.removeMessage(null)` updates
`lastConsumeTimestamp`, computes `queueOffsetMax + 1` for a nonempty ready map,
then catches the null-list exception. The queue entries and count/size values
remain unchanged. Rust now exposes `remove_message_nullable`; `None` updates the
consume timestamp and returns the current next offset without modifying the
queue.

The invoked Java facade fixture and Rust comparison check next offset,
timestamp update, count, size, and tree. Fixture SHA-256:
`357c266f6bea2c4df5b066d334b75b28314202d1d198a34bd270115345b9096f`.

